        "created_at": "2014-12-30T12:56:38.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"payprplayn\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/p/b2d939/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> payprplayn:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If Citizen Truth \"becomes the defender\" of an attack, does that mean range and line of sight are figured to him, or merely that the damage comes toward him, to be blocked by his defense/power?&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>He rolls defense and takes damage. (And applies any abilities that refer to him being the defender.) &nbsp;Line of Sight and Range aren't recalculated.</p>",
